  "prompt": "You are writing the control policy for a peg-in-hole insertion cell.\n\nA UR5e arm holds a square peg (20 x 20 mm, 80 mm long) pointing straight down. A block on the table\nhas a square hole (21 x 21 mm, 0.5 mm clearance per side, 50 mm deep); its top surface is at z = 0.05 m.\nIn our test cell the hole is placed at x = 0.45 +/- 0.05 m, y = 0.00 +/- 0.05 m, yaw = 0 +/- 15 degrees.\nThe trial succeeds when the peg is seated at least 30 mm deep in the hole with less than 1 mm lateral error.\n\nWrite a Python module that defines `def run(api):`. It is called once per trial and must return when\nfinished. `api` is the module below; use only these four functions (plus `math`, which you may import).\nYou have at most 300 API calls per trial. Contact force above 150 N aborts the trial as a collision.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The four functions a policy may call. A policy is `def run(api): ...` and receives this module.\n\nUnits: metres and degrees in the world frame; z is up and the table top is z = 0.\nThe robot holds a 20 x 20 mm square peg, 80 mm long, pointing straight down. The peg tip is the\ncontrolled point. The hole is a 21 x 21 mm square, 50 mm deep, cut into the top of a 50 mm-high block.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n_SIM = None  # set by the trial runner\n\n\ndef hole_pose():\n    \"\"\"Camera estimate of the hole: returns ((x, y, z_top_surface), yaw_deg).\n    Yaw is the rotation of the square hole about z, reported in [-45, 45) because a square repeats every 90 degrees.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.hole_pose()\n\n\ndef move_to(xyz, yaw_deg):\n    \"\"\"Move the peg tip to xyz (metres) with the peg rotated yaw_deg about z, peg pointing down.\n    Joint-space motion; blocks until the arm has settled. Moving into the block is a collision.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.move_to(xyz, yaw_deg)\n\n\ndef step_down(mm):\n    \"\"\"Lower the peg tip by mm millimetres from the last commanded target (negative values raise it).\n    Returns the contact force on the peg in newtons after the motion settles.\n    The run is aborted as a collision if the contact force ever exceeds 150 N.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.step_down(mm)\n\n\ndef done():\n    \"\"\"True if the peg tip is at least 30 mm below the block's top surface (i.e. seated in the hole).\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.done()\n\n```\n\nReply with the complete module in a single ```python code block, followed by at most three sentences\nexplaining the strategy.",
  "response": "```python\nimport math\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    \"\"\"Force-monitored insertion with bounded, above-surface alignment retries.\"\"\"\n    calls = 0\n\n    def call(function, *args):\n        nonlocal calls\n        calls += 1\n        return function(*args)\n\n    (cx, cy, top), camera_yaw = call(api.hole_pose)\n\n    if not all(math.isfinite(v) for v in (cx, cy, top, camera_yaw)):\n        return\n\n    safe_z = top + 0.060\n    hover_z = top + 0.001\n    force_limit = 15.0\n    target_z = safe_z\n\n    def acceptable_force(force):\n        return math.isfinite(force) and abs(force) < force_limit\n\n    def lower(mm):\n        nonlocal target_z\n        # step_down uses the commanded target, not the achieved position.\n        target_z -= mm * 0.001\n        return call(api.step_down, mm)\n\n    def retract():\n        nonlocal target_z\n        raise_mm = (safe_z - target_z) * 1000.0\n        call(api.step_down, -raise_mm)\n        target_z = safe_z\n\n    def candidates():\n        # First correct modest yaw error at the camera's estimated centre.\n        for dyaw in (0.0, -2.0, 2.0, -4.0, 4.0):\n            yield 0.0, 0.0, dyaw\n\n        # Search translation in the hole's local coordinate system.\n        spacing = 0.0006\n        for radius in (1, 2, 3):\n            offsets = [\n                (i, j)\n                for i in range(-radius, radius + 1)\n                for j in range(-radius, radius + 1)\n                if max(abs(i), abs(j)) == radius\n            ]\n            offsets.sort(key=lambda p: p[0] * p[0] + p[1] * p[1])\n            for dyaw in (0.0, -2.0, 2.0):\n                for i, j in offsets:\n                    yield i * spacing, j * spacing, dyaw\n\n    angle = math.radians(camera_yaw)\n    c, s = math.cos(angle), math.sin(angle)\n\n    call(api.move_to, (cx, cy, safe_z), camera_yaw)\n\n    for dx, dy, dyaw in candidates():\n        # A complete attempt, including insertion and retraction, uses\n        # at most 78 calls. This gate keeps the total below 300.\n        if calls > 220:\n            return\n\n        x = cx + c * dx - s * dy\n        y = cy + s * dx + c * dy\n        yaw = (camera_yaw + dyaw + 45.0) % 90.0 - 45.0\n\n        # Change lateral position and yaw only after retracting fully.\n        call(api.move_to, (x, y, safe_z), yaw)\n        call(api.move_to, (x, y, hover_z), yaw)\n        target_z = hover_z\n\n        # Reach the nominal surface, then probe in 0.2 mm increments.\n        force = lower(1.0)\n        clear = acceptable_force(force)\n        if clear:\n            for _ in range(5):\n                force = lower(0.2)\n                if not acceptable_force(force):\n                    clear = False\n                    break\n\n        if not clear:\n            retract()\n            continue\n\n        # The tip is commanded 1 mm inside: continue without lateral motion.\n        seated = False\n        for step in range(62):\n            force = lower(0.5)\n            commanded_depth_mm = 1.0 + 0.5 * (step + 1)\n\n            if not acceptable_force(force):\n                seated = bool(call(api.done))\n                break\n\n            if commanded_depth_mm >= 30.0:\n                if call(api.done):\n                    seated = True\n                    break\n\n        if seated:\n            return\n\n        retract()\n```\n\nThe policy aligns to the camera estimate, probes gently, and retries nearby translations and yaw angles only after retracting above the block. It reserves enough calls for insertion and checks completion at seating depth. Because camera-error bounds and contact stiffness are unspecified, small steps and an early force threshold reduce risk but cannot guarantee avoiding the 150 N abort threshold.",
  "code": "import math\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    \"\"\"Force-monitored insertion with bounded, above-surface alignment retries.\"\"\"\n    calls = 0\n\n    def call(function, *args):\n        nonlocal calls\n        calls += 1\n        return function(*args)\n\n    (cx, cy, top), camera_yaw = call(api.hole_pose)\n\n    if not all(math.isfinite(v) for v in (cx, cy, top, camera_yaw)):\n        return\n\n    safe_z = top + 0.060\n    hover_z = top + 0.001\n    force_limit = 15.0\n    target_z = safe_z\n\n    def acceptable_force(force):\n        return math.isfinite(force) and abs(force) < force_limit\n\n    def lower(mm):\n        nonlocal target_z\n        # step_down uses the commanded target, not the achieved position.\n        target_z -= mm * 0.001\n        return call(api.step_down, mm)\n\n    def retract():\n        nonlocal target_z\n        raise_mm = (safe_z - target_z) * 1000.0\n        call(api.step_down, -raise_mm)\n        target_z = safe_z\n\n    def candidates():\n        # First correct modest yaw error at the camera's estimated centre.\n        for dyaw in (0.0, -2.0, 2.0, -4.0, 4.0):\n            yield 0.0, 0.0, dyaw\n\n        # Search translation in the hole's local coordinate system.\n        spacing = 0.0006\n        for radius in (1, 2, 3):\n            offsets = [\n                (i, j)\n                for i in range(-radius, radius + 1)\n                for j in range(-radius, radius + 1)\n                if max(abs(i), abs(j)) == radius\n            ]\n            offsets.sort(key=lambda p: p[0] * p[0] + p[1] * p[1])\n            for dyaw in (0.0, -2.0, 2.0):\n                for i, j in offsets:\n                    yield i * spacing, j * spacing, dyaw\n\n    angle = math.radians(camera_yaw)\n    c, s = math.cos(angle), math.sin(angle)\n\n    call(api.move_to, (cx, cy, safe_z), camera_yaw)\n\n    for dx, dy, dyaw in candidates():\n        # A complete attempt, including insertion and retraction, uses\n        # at most 78 calls. This gate keeps the total below 300.\n        if calls > 220:\n            return\n\n        x = cx + c * dx - s * dy\n        y = cy + s * dx + c * dy\n        yaw = (camera_yaw + dyaw + 45.0) % 90.0 - 45.0\n\n        # Change lateral position and yaw only after retracting fully.\n        call(api.move_to, (x, y, safe_z), yaw)\n        call(api.move_to, (x, y, hover_z), yaw)\n        target_z = hover_z\n\n        # Reach the nominal surface, then probe in 0.2 mm increments.\n        force = lower(1.0)\n        clear = acceptable_force(force)\n        if clear:\n            for _ in range(5):\n                force = lower(0.2)\n                if not acceptable_force(force):\n                    clear = False\n                    break\n\n        if not clear:\n            retract()\n            continue\n\n        # The tip is commanded 1 mm inside: continue without lateral motion.\n        seated = False\n        for step in range(62):\n            force = lower(0.5)\n            commanded_depth_mm = 1.0 + 0.5 * (step + 1)\n\n            if not acceptable_force(force):\n                seated = bool(call(api.done))\n                break\n\n            if commanded_depth_mm >= 30.0:\n                if call(api.done):\n                    seated = True\n                    break\n\n        if seated:\n            return\n\n        retract()\n",
